mes</th><td class="infobox-data">Hare-lip, cleft lip and palate</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" class="infobox-full-data"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="./File:Cleftlipandpalate.JPG" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="./File:Cleftlipandpalate.JPG" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Cleftlipandpalate.JPG/250px-Cleftlipandpalate.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Cleftlipandpalate.JPG/500px-Cleftlipandpalate.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1839" data-file-height="2509" data-file-type="bitmap" height="300" width="220" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" class="infobox-full-data">Child with incomplete unilateral cleft lip</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Medical_specialty" title="Medical specialty">Specialty</a></th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Oral_and_Maxillofacial_Surgery" title="Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery" class="mw-redirect">Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Otorhinolaryngology" title="Otorhinolaryngology">Otorhinolaryngology</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Pediatrics" title="Pediatrics">pediatrics</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Signs_and_symptoms" title="Signs and symptoms">Symptoms</a></th><td class="infobox-data">Opening in the upper lip that may extend into the nose or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Palate" title="Palate">palate</a><sup about="#mwt6" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwCA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCg">[<