a"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Smoking_and_pregnancy" title="Smoking and pregnancy">Smoking during pregnancy</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Diabetes_mellitus_and_pregnancy" title="Diabetes mellitus and pregnancy" class="mw-redirect">diabetes</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Obesity" title="Obesity">obesity</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Advanced_maternal_age" title="Advanced maternal age">older mother</a>, certain <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Drugs_in_pregnancy" title="Drugs in pregnancy">medications</a><sup about="#mwt14" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt18" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Wat2014_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Wat2014"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Wat2014-2"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-Wat2014-2" id="mwHA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Treatment</th><td class="infobox-data">Surgery, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Speech_therapy" title="Speech therapy" class="mw-redirect">speech therapy</a>, dental care<sup about="#mwt21" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwIA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Prognosis" title="Prognosis">Prognosis</a></th><td class="infobox-data">Good (with treatment)<sup about="#mwt23" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwJA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Frequency</th><td class="infobox-data">1.5 per 1000 births (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Developed_world" title="Developed world" class="mw-redirect">developed world</a>)<sup about="#mwt25" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Wat2014_2-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Wat2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-Wat2014-2" id="mwKA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Deaths</th><td class="infobox-data">3,800 (2017)<sup about="#mwt27" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Roth2017_3-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Roth2017"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-Roth2017-3" id="mwLA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLg">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr></tbody></table><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt4"><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1236303919" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt29" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Infobox/styles-images.css"}}'>@media screen{html.skin-theme-clientpref-night .mw-parser-output .infobox-has-images-with-white-backgrounds img{background:white}}@media screen and (prefers-color-scheme:dark){html.skin-theme-clientpref-os .mw-parser-output .infobox-has-images-with-white-backgrounds img{background:white}}</style></span>

<p id="mwMA"><b id="mwMQ">Cleft lip</b> (<b id="mwMg">orofacial cleft</b>) is a medical condition where the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Upper_lip" title="Upper lip" class="mw-redirect" id="mwMw">upper lip</a> has an opening from the perimeter of the mouth, that may extend into the nose.<sup about="#mwt30" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwNA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">]</span></span></a></sup> The opening may be on one side, both sides, or in the middle.<sup about="#mwt31" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwOA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwOQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOw">]</span></span></a></sup>  <b id="mwPA">Cleft palate</b> is an associated condition where the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Palate" title="Palate" id="mwPQ">palate</a> (the roof of the mouth) has an opening into the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Nasal_cavity" title="Nasal cavity" id="mwPg">nose</a>.<sup about="#mwt32" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQQ">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQg">]</span></span></a></sup> The term <b id="mwQw">orofacial cleft</b> refers to either condition or to both occurring together. These conditions can result in feeding problems, speech problems, hearing problems, and frequent <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Otitis_media" title="Otitis media" id="mwRA">ear infections</a>.<sup about="#mwt33" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwRQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwRg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSA">]</span></span></a></sup> The condition may be associated with other disorders.<sup about="#mwt36" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CDC2014-1"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwSQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwSg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<!-- Cause, mechanism, and diagnosis -->
<p id="mwTQ">Cleft lip and palate are the result of tissues of the face not joining properly during <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Prenatal_development" title="Prenatal development" id="mwTg">development</a>.<sup about="#mwt37" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwTw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwUA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUQ">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUg">]</span></span></a></sup> As such, they are a type of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Congenital_deformity" title="Congenital deformity" class="mw-redirect" id="mwUw">birth defect</a>.<sup about="#mwt38" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwVQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVw">]</span></span></a></sup> The cause is unknown in most cases.<sup about="#mwt39" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwWA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWw">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Risk_factor_(epidemiology)" title="Risk factor (epidemiology)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwXA">Risk factors</a> include <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Smoking_and_pregnancy" title="Smoking and pregnancy" id="mwXQ">smoking during pregnancy</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Diabetes_mellitus_and_pregnancy" title="Diabetes mellitus and pregnancy" class="mw-redirect" id="mwXg">diabetes</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Obesity" title="Obesity" id="mwXw">obesity</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Advanced_maternal_age" title="Advanced maternal age" id="mwYA">an older mother</a>, and certain <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Drugs_in_pregnancy" title="Drugs in pregnancy" id="mwYQ">medications</a> (such as some used to treat <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Seizures" title="Seizures" class="mw-redirect" id="mwYg">seizures</a>).<sup about="#mwt40" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwYw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwZA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZQ">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt41" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Wat2014_2-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Wat2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-Wat2014-2" id="mwZw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwaA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaQ">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwag">]</span></span></a></sup> Cleft lip and cleft palate can often be diagnosed during pregnancy with an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Obstetric_ultrasonography" title="Obstetric ultrasonography" id="mwaw">ultrasound exam</a>.<sup about="#mwt42" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwbA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwbQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<!-- Treatment -->
<p id="mwcA">A cleft lip or palate can be successfully treated with surgery.<sup about="#mwt43" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwcQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdA">]</span></span></a></sup> This is often done in the first few months of life for cleft lip and before eighteen months for cleft palate.<sup about="#mwt44" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-18" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwdQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mweA">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Speech_therapy" title="Speech therapy" class="mw-redirect" id="mweQ">Speech therapy</a> and dental care may also be needed.<sup about="#mwt45" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-19" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mweg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwew"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfQ">]</span></span></a></sup> With appropriate treatment, outcomes are good.<sup about="#mwt46" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CDC2014_1-20" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CDC2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-CDC2014-1" id="mwfg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<!-- Epidemiology and society--><p id="mwgg">
Cleft lip and palate occurs in about 1 to 2 per 1000 births in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Developed_world" title="Developed world" class="mw-redirect" id="mwgw">developed world</a>.<sup about="#mwt49" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Wat2014_2-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Wat2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-Wat2014-2" id="mwhA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwhQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhw">]</span></span></a></sup> Cleft lip is about twice as common in males as females, while cleft palate without cleft lip is more common in females.<sup about="#mwt50" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Wat2014_2-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Wat2014"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-Wat2014-2" id="mwiA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwiQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwig">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiw">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2017, it resulted in about 3,800 deaths globally, down from 14,600 deaths in 1990.<sup about="#mwt53" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Roth2017_3-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Roth2017"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Roth2017-3"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-Roth2017-3" id="mwjA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwjQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjg">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt56" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_4-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-4"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-:0-4" id="mwkA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwkQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkw">]</span></span></a></sup> Cleft lips are commonly known as <b id="mwlA">hare-lips</b> because of their resemblance to the lips of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Hare" title="Hare" id="mwlQ">hares</a> or rabbits, although that term is considered to be offensive in certain contexts.<sup about="#mwt59" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-5" id="mwlg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwlw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwmA">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwmQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p> <span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt47" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"TOC limit","href":"./Template:TOC_limit"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}' id="mwmg"><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r886046785" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt48" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:TOC limit/styles.css"}}'>.mw-parser-output .toclimit-2 .toclevel-1 ul,.mw-parser-output .toclimit-3 .toclevel-2 ul,.mw-parser-output .toclimit-4 .toclevel-3 ul,.mw-parser-output .toclimit-5 .toclevel-4 ul,.mw-parser-output .toclimit-6 .toclevel-5 ul,.mw-parser-output .toclimit-7 .toclevel-6 ul{display:none}</style></span><div class="toclimit-3" about="#mwt47" id="mwmw"><meta property="mw:PageProp/toc"/></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwnA"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Signs_and_symptoms">Signs and symptoms</h2>

<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwnQ"><h3 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Cleft_lip">Cleft lip</h3>
<p id="mwng">If the cleft does not affect the palate structure of the mouth, it is referred to as cleft lip.  Cleft lip is formed in the top of the lip as either a small gap or an indentation in the lip (partial or incomplete cleft), or it continues into the nose (complete cleft). Lip cleft can occur as a one-sided (unilateral) or two-sided (bilateral) condition. It is due to the failure of fusion of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Maxillary_prominence" title="Maxillary prominence" id="mwnw">maxillary prominence</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Frontonasal_process#Nasal_processes" title="Frontonasal process" id="mwoA">medial nasal processes</a> (formation of the primary palate).</p>

<ul class="gallery mw-gallery-traditional center" typeof="mw:Extension/gallery" about="#mwt60" data-mw='{"name":"gallery","attrs":{"class":"center","widths":"150px","heights":"150px"},"body":{}}' id="mwoQ">
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 185px;" id="mwog"><div class="thumb" style="width: 180px; height: 180px;" id="mwow"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwpA"><a href="./File:CleftLip1.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="Unilateral incomplete" id="mwpQ"><img resource="./File:CleftLip1.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/CleftLip1.svg/250px-CleftLip1.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/CleftLip1.svg/330px-CleftLip1.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Unilateral incomplete" data-file-width="149" data-file-height="150" data-file-type="drawing" height="150" width="149" class="mw-file-element" id="mwpg"/></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwpw">Unilateral incomplete</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 185px;" id="mwqA"><div class="thumb" style="width: 180px; height: 180px;" id="mwqQ"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwqg"><a href="./File:Cleftlip2.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="Unilateral complete" id="mwqw"><img resource="./File:Cleftlip2.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Cleftlip2.svg/250px-Cleftlip2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Cleftlip2.svg/330px-Cleftlip2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Unilateral complete" data-file-width="116" data-file-height="116" data-file-type="drawing" height="150" width="150" class="mw-file-element" id="mwrA"/></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwrQ">Unilateral complete</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 185px;" id="mwrg"><div class="thumb" style="width: 180px; height: 180px;" id="mwrw"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwsA"><a href="./File:CleftLip3.png" class="mw-file-description" title="Bilateral complete" id="mwsQ"><img resource="./File:CleftLip3.png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2d/CleftLip3.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Bilateral complete" data-file-width="150" data-file-height="150" data-file-type="bitmap" height="150" width="150" class="mw-file-element" id="mwsg"/></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwsw">Bilateral complete</div></li>
</ul>

<p id="mwtA">A mild form of a cleft lip is a microform cleft.<sup about="#mwt64" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-6"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-6" id="mwtQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtw">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuA">]</span></span></a></sup> A microform cleft can appear as small as a little dent in the red part of the lip or look like a scar from the lip up to the nostril.<sup about="#mwt67" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-7"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-7" id="mwuQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwug"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuw">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvA">]</span></span></a></sup> In some cases <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Orbicularis_oris_muscle" title="Orbicularis oris muscle" id="mwvQ">muscle tissue in the lip</a> underneath the scar is affected and might require reconstructive surgery.<sup about="#mwt70" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-8"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-8" id="mwvg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwwA">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwwQ">]</span></span></a></sup> It is advised to have newborn infants with a microform cleft checked with a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Craniofacial_team" title="Craniofacial team" class="mw-redirect" id="mwwg">craniofacial team</a> as soon as possible to determine the severity of the cleft.<sup about="#mwt73" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-9"}}'><a href="./Cleft_lip_and_cleft_palate#cite_note-9" id="mwww"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwxA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxQ">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<ul class="gallery mw-gallery-traditional center" typeof="mw:Extension/gallery" about="#mwt74" data-mw='{"name":"gallery","attrs":{"class":"center","widths":"150","heights":"150"},"body":{}}' id="mwxw">
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 185px;" id="mwyA"><div class="thumb" style="width: 180px; height: 180px;" id="mwyQ"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwyg"><a href="./File:13900470_3PREOPERATION0.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Six-month-old girl before going into surgery to have her unilateral complete cleft lip repaired" id="mwyw"><img resource="./File:13900470_3PREOPERATION0.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/13900470_3PREOPERATION0.jpg/250px-13900470_3PREOPERATION0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/13900470_3PREOPERATION0.jpg/330px-13900470_3PREOPERATION0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Six-month-old girl before going into surgery to have her unilateral complete cleft lip repaired" data-file-width="653" data-file-height="685" data-file-type="bitmap" height="150" width="143" class="mw-file-element" id="mwzA"/></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwzQ">Six-month-old girl before going into surgery to have her unilateral complete cleft lip repaired</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 185px;" id="mwzg"><div class="thumb" style="width: 180px; height: 180px;" id="mwzw"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mw0A"><a href="./File:10-month-old_girl_showing_scar_from_facial_reconstruction_surgery_for_cleft_lip.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="The same girl, one month after the surgery" id="mw0Q"><img resource="./File:10-month-old_girl_showing_scar_from_facial_reconstruction_surgery_for_cleft_lip.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/10-month-old_girl_showing_scar_from_facial_reconstruction_surgery_for_cleft_lip.jpg/120px-10-month-old_girl_showing_scar_from_facial_reconstruction_surgery_for_cleft_lip.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/10-month-old_girl_showing_scar_from_facial_reconstruction_surgery_for_cleft_lip.jpg/250px-10-month-old_girl_showing_scar_from_facial_reconstruction_surgery_for_cleft_lip.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="The same girl, one month after the surgery" data-file-width="600" data-file-height="800" data-file-type="bitmap" height="150" width="112" class="mw-file-element" id="mw0g"/></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mw0w">The same girl, one month after the surgery</div></li>
